From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anas <273038692+amas-cd@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 01:30:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] totk: a mod module's reads of cntfrq_el0 answer the console's
 19.2 MHz

TOTK Online reads the counter frequency itself (25 sites) to turn ticks into time. The rewrite sends cntpct/cntvct to
the gate, which counts at the Switch's 19.2 MHz, but left cntfrq_el0 to the Mac's own register: 1,000,000,000 on this
Apple silicon. Every span the mod measured was 52 times too short (its clock almost stopped): the other players'
movement, its timeouts. Each read now branches to three words after the image that load 19,200,000.

Seen in the log ("25 read(s) of the counter frequency now answer..."), the game starts and exchanges with the server
as before; not yet tried with another player.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 games/totk/runtime/loader.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/games/totk/runtime/loader.c b/games/totk/runtime/loader.c
index a4adea9a5943d902f4672934757cdf48aabe12dc..7581fd42bb34f24cebe45414c2e7b2da7cb8b23c 100644
--- a/games/totk/runtime/loader.c
+++ b/games/totk/runtime/loader.c
@@ -528,6 +528,26 @@ static int stale_target_reference(int num,siginfo_t *info,ucontext_t *u){
 }
 #endif
 #if !TARGET_OS_IPHONE
+/* A mod module reads the counter's frequency itself (mrs xN, cntfrq_el0: 25 sites in TOTK Online, libnx-style "ticks to
+   nanoseconds") and that read ran on the Mac's own register: 1,000,000,000 on this Apple silicon, 19,200,000 on the console,
+   while the counter it divides is the gate's 19.2 MHz one (runtime_dispatch). Every span the mod measured was 52 times too
+   short: its interpolation of the other players, its timeouts and its send pacing ran on a clock almost stopped. Each read
+   becomes a branch to three words in the zero bytes after the image, in the executable patch area (movz/movk the console's
+   frequency, branch back). The retail modules never read the register (their SDK has the constant). */
+static void mod_counter_frequency(Module *m){
+ if(m->ctor_flag)return;
+ size_t end=page_up(m->file_size),room=(end-m->file_size)/12;unsigned n=0,left=0;
+ for(uint64_t o=0;o+4<=m->text_end;o+=4){uint32_t w;memcpy(&w,m->base+o,4);
+  if((w&0xffffffe0)!=0xd53be000)continue;
+  unsigned rt=w&31;uint64_t s=end-12*(uint64_t)(n+1);uint32_t z[3]={0,0,0};
+  if(rt==31||n>=room||memcmp(m->base+s,z,12)){left++;continue;}
+  uint32_t c[3]={0xd29f0000|rt,0xf2a02480|rt,0x14000000|(uint32_t)(((int64_t)(o+4)-(int64_t)(s+8))>>2&0x3ffffff)};   /* movz xN,#0xf800; movk xN,#0x124,lsl #16 (19,200,000); b back */
+  uint32_t j=0x14000000|(uint32_t)(((int64_t)s-(int64_t)o)>>2&0x3ffffff);
+  memcpy(m->base+s,c,12);memcpy(m->base+o,&j,4);n++;}
+ if(n||left)fprintf(stderr,"[totk] %s: %u read(s) of the counter frequency now answer the console's 19.2 MHz (%u left as they were)\n",m->name,n,left);
+}
+#endif
+#if !TARGET_OS_IPHONE
 /* Diagnostic for a mod module (2026-11-28, TOTK Online: a hit received from another player did nothing on the Mac and the
    mod's release build drops its own log lines). TOTK_MOD_DIAG, else the file
    ~/Library/Application Support/MacNativeGames/TOTK/mod-diag.txt, lists sites separated by commas, spaces or new lines; the
@@ -893,6 +913,7 @@ int main(int argc,char **argv) {
  for(unsigned i=0;i<NM;i++)map_module(&modules[i],argv[1]);
  for(unsigned i=0;i<NM;i++)relocate(&modules[i]);
 #if !TARGET_OS_IPHONE
+ for(unsigned i=0;i<NM;i++)mod_counter_frequency(&modules[i]);
  mod_diag_install();
 #endif
  rtld_module_list();
